      "), {'query': 'Train and evaluate the bert-base-uncased model on the SST-2 dataset using the AMP method. Report the maximum test accuracy as a json structured as follows: {\"max_test_acc\": 0.0} (replace 0.0 with the actual value).\\n\\nAdditional instructions:\\n1. Only load the first 10 examples of each (training/validation/test) set in the dataset.\\n2. Train only one batch.\\n\\nGit repository: https://github.com/pai-smallisallyourneed/mixup-amp', 'github_repo': 'https://github.com/pai-smallisallyourneed/mixup-amp', 'git_commit': '55ba0ebd9573d0a0f7aaa225f07b280900fb2431', 'trajectory': '[[ ## thought_0 ## ]]\\nFirst, I need to explore the repository to identify the training and evaluation pipeline, as well as how datasets are loaded, to determine where to make adjustments to: (1) use bert-base-uncased, (2) train on SST-2, (3) limit to 10 examples per split, (4) train only one batch, and (5) ensure AMP (Automatic Mixed Precision) is used. I\\'ll start by listing the files in the repository to look for main scripts related to training and dataset loading.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_0 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_0 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"ls -l /workspace\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_0 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 0\\\\ntotal 0\", \"message\": \"executed in 0.01sec\\\\nProcess finished and cleaned\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_1 ## ]]\\nThe repository root is empty, which suggests that the code might be located within subdirectories. I need to list all files and folders recursively to identify the location of training scripts and data loading code.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_1 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_1 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"find /workspace -type f | sort\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_1 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 0\", \"message\": \"executed in 0.01sec\\\\nProcess finished and cleaned\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_2 ## ]]\\nThe output from the find command is empty, which suggests that either the files have not been checked out correctly, or the repository contents are not loaded. To confirm whether the expected repo content exists, I should check the git status and possibly git log to gather clues. This will clarify if the files are present but perhaps not checked out in /workspace due to a subdirectory or similar.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_2 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_2 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"git status\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_2 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 128\\\\nfatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git\", \"message\": \"executed in 0.01sec\\\\nProcess finished and cleaned\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_3 ## ]]\\nThe workspace does not currently contain the files from the repository; there are no files present and git is not initialized. It appears I need to clone the repository into the workspace and check out the specified commit to access the codebase before proceeding with any modifications or running code.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_3 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_3 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"git clone https://github.com/pai-smallisallyourneed/mixup-amp /workspace/mixup-amp && cd /workspace/mixup-amp && git checkout 55ba0ebd9573d0a0f7aaa225f07b280900fb2431\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_3 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 0\\\\nCloning into \\'/workspace/mixup-amp\\'...\\\\nNote: switching to \\'55ba0ebd9573d0a0f7aaa225f07b280900fb2431\\'.\\\\n\\\\nYou are in \\'detached HEAD\\' state. You can look around, make experimental\\\\nchanges and commit them, and you can discard any commits you make in this\\\\nstate without impacting any branches by switching back to a branch.\\\\n\\\\nIf you want to create a new branch to retain commits you create, you may\\\\ndo so (now or later) by using -c with the switch command. Example:\\\\n\\\\n  git switch -c <new-branch-name>\\\\n\\\\nOr undo this operation with:\\\\n\\\\n  git switch -\\\\n\\\\nTurn off this advice by setting config variable advice.detachedHead to false\\\\n\\\\nHEAD is now at 55ba0eb Update README.md\", \"message\": \"executed in 1.2sec\\\\nProcess finished and cleaned\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_4 ## ]]\\nThe repository is now cloned and checked out to the given commit. I need to list the files in the `/workspace/mixup-amp` directory to identify the main training script(s) and dataset setup logic so I can plan targeted modifications for the SST-2, AMP, batching, and limited-sample requirements.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_4 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_4 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"ls -l /workspace/mixup-amp\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_4 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 0\\\\ntotal 76\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  1118 Oct 20 03:08 LICENSE\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root   969 Oct 20 03:08 README.md\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 26891 Oct 20 03:08 data_loader.py\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 17121 Oct 20 03:08 model.py\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root    54 Oct 20 03:08 requirements.txt\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 16019 Oct 20 03:08 run_main.py\", \"message\": \"executed in 0.01sec\\\\nProcess finished and cleaned\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_5 ## ]]\\nThe main training script is likely `run_main.py`, with supporting files `data_loader.py` and `model.py`. My next step is to examine `run_main.py` for the overall workflow—especially how it loads the dataset, selects the model, configures AMP, and performs training and evaluation—so I can identify where to (1) switch to SST-2, (2) limit splits to 10 samples each, (3) run only one batch, and (4) enable AMP. I will read the initial lines and look for the main function and argument parsing.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_5 ## ]]\\nread_file\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_5 ## ]]\\n{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/mixup-amp/run_main.py\", \"lines_start\": 1, \"lines_end\": 60}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_5 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": false, \"error\": \"File not found: /workspace/mixup-amp/run_main.py\", \"suggestions\": [\"Check if the file path is correct\", \"Ensure the file exists in the working directory\"]}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_6 ## ]]\\nThe error indicates that `/workspace/mixup-amp/run_main.py` cannot be found, but the previous `ls -l` output shows the file exists in that location. There may have been a temporary filesystem issue or typo. I\\'ll retry reading the file to check its content and ensure the path is correct.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_6 ## ]]\\nread_file\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_6 ## ]]\\n{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/mixup-amp/run_main.py\", \"lines_start\": 1, \"lines_end\": 60}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_6 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": false, \"error\": \"File not found: /workspace/mixup-amp/run_main.py\", \"suggestions\": [\"Check if the file path is correct\", \"Ensure the file exists in the working directory\"]}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_7 ## ]]\\nThe file /workspace/mixup-amp/run_main.py is listed by ls but cannot be read, possibly due to a file system synchronization issue or permissions. To troubleshoot, I should attempt to read a different listed file (such as README.md) to determine if the issue affects all files or just run_main.py. This will help clarify the cause and next steps.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_7 ## ]]\\nread_file\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_7 ## ]]\\n{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/mixup-amp/README.md\", \"lines_start\": 1, \"lines_end\": 40}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_7 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": false, \"error\": \"File not found: /workspace/mixup-amp/README.md\", \"suggestions\": [\"Check if the file path is correct\", \"Ensure the file exists in the working directory\"]}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_8 ## ]]\\nThere may be a technical issue in accessing the files in the `/workspace/mixup-amp` directory, despite the fact that `ls` can list them. As a next debugging step, I will use the `cat` command via the shell to directly read the contents of `/workspace/mixup-amp/run_main.py`. If that succeeds, I\\'ll know it\\'s an API issue with `read_file`, and can proceed with shell-based reads instead.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_8 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_8 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"c