lly, I must check if the scripts accept `linkbert-base` as a model name and where it should be referenced/changed. \\n\\nFirst, I\\'ll look for where available Hugging Face models (especially LinkBERT-base) are referenced in the codebase. I\\'ll search for occurrences of \\'linkbert\\' or \\'LinkBERT\\' in the `dpt` folder, as that\\'s where training scripts are. This will confirm if and how LinkBERT is supported.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_12 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_12 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"grep -ir \\'linkbert\\' /workspace/dpt\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_12 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 1\", \"message\": \"executed in 0.01sec\\\\nProcess finished and cleaned\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_13 ## ]]\\nThere were no occurrences of \\'linkbert\\' in the `/workspace/dpt` directory, which suggests LinkBERT is not hardcoded, but instead, the model selection is made via the `--model_name` CLI argument (passed to Hugging Face\\'s AutoTokenizer and presumably AutoModel). LinkBERT-base should therefore be specified as `--model_name \\'sentence-transformers/LinkBERT-base\\'` (the Hugging Face model hub ID).\\n\\nBefore fine-tuning, I need to:\\n1. Download and preprocess the SQuAD MRQA dataset (first 10 examples of train, eval/dev, and test).\\n2. Confirm how data preprocessing is done in the project. There may be a script or code for MRQA-style JSONL preprocessing. I\\'ll search for \\'preprocess\\' and \\'jsonl\\' in `/workspace/dpt` to find a relevant script or function.\\n\\nFirst, I\\'ll search for the keyword \"preprocess\" in `/workspace/dpt` to locate the preprocessing script.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_13 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_13 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"grep -irl \\'preprocess\\' /workspace/dpt\"}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_13 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 2\\\\ngrep: /workspace/dpt: No such file or directory\", \"message\": \"executed in 0.01sec\\\\nProcess finished and cleaned\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_14 ## ]]\