tils.py` directly, since this file is likely to contain data loading and preprocessing functions needed for handling MRQA SQuAD JSONL files.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_16 ## ]]\\nread_file\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_16 ## ]]\\n{\"file_path\": \"/workspace/dpt/data_utils.py\", \"lines_start\": 1, \"lines_end\": 60}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_16 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": false, \"error\": \"File not found: /workspace/dpt/data_utils.py\", \"suggestions\": [\"Check if the file path is correct\", \"Ensure the file exists in the working directory\"]}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_17 ## ]]\\nThere appears to be an inconsistency in file visibility between shell command listings and direct file reads. Since all the relevant training, data processing, and evaluation files should be present in the workspace as per earlier listings, but shell access to `/workspace/dpt` now fails, I should check if the current working directory has changed or if there is a symlink or mapping issue. I\\'ll list the current working directory and its immediate subdirectories/files to verify their accessibility and ensure I use the correct file paths moving forward.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_17 ## ]]\\nrun_command\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_17 ## ]]\\n{\"command\": \"pwd && ls -la\", \"timeout\": 10}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_17 ## ]]\\n{\"success\": true, \"output\": \"Exit code: 0\\\\n/workspace\\\\ntotal 152\\\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  4096 Oct 20 03:23 .\\\\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root  4096 Oct 20 03:18 ..\\\\ndrwxr-xr-x 8 root root  4096 Oct 20 03:22 .git\\\\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 root root  4096 Oct 20 03:22 .github\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  1799 Oct 20 03:22 .gitignore\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  1066 Oct 20 03:22 LICENSE\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  7315 Oct 20 03:22 README.md\\\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 root root  4096 Oct 20 03:22 data\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root 79902 Oct 20 03:22 diagram.png\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  3964 Oct 20 03:23 entailment-data.zip\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  9448 Oct 20 03:23 entailment-formatted.json\\\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 root root  