      "ValueError: ('Failed to parse response as per signature from original completion with input', '[[ ## next_thought ## ]]\\nI have the full content of \"AT_finetuning.py\" and will now prepare a modified version:\\n- Limit languages to [\\'portuguese\\']\\n- Use only question_type=[\\'standard\\']\\n- Use model_names=[\\'bert-base-uncased\\'] only\\n- Set batch_size=1\\n- Set num_train_epochs=1\\n- Restrict train/validation/test loading to .head(10) for first 10 rows from each split\\n\\nI\\'ll write the modified script back to \"Pira/Triggering/AT_finetuning.py\". Afterward, I will confirm the presence of the required dataset CSVs (\"train.csv\", \"validation.csv\", \"test.csv\") in \"Pira/Data\" before running the experiment.\\nFor now, I\\'ll proceed to write the edited script.\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_name ## ]]\\nwrite_file\\n\\n[[ ## next_tool_args ## ]]\\n{\\n  \"file_path\": \"Pira/Triggering/AT_finetuning.py\",\\n  \"content\": \"import pandas as pd\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\nfrom datasets import Dataset, DatasetDict\\\\nimport csv\\\\nfrom sklearn.metrics import f1_score, accuracy_score\\\\n\\\\n## Parameters\\\\nlanguages = [\\'portuguese\\']\\\\nquestion_type = [\\'standard\\']\\\\nmodel_names = [\\'bert-base-uncased\\']\\\\n\\\\n# Create headline\\\\nwith open(\\'AT_results.csv\\', \\'w\\') as fd:\\\\n    write = csv.writer(fd)\\\\n    write.writerow([\\'model_name\\', \\'dataset_type\\', \\'language\\', \\'f1\\', \\'acc\\'])\\\\n\\\\nfor language in languages:\\\\n    for model_name in model_names:\\\\n        batch_size = 1\\\\n        for questions in question_type:\\\\n            train = pd.read_csv(\\'../Data/train.csv\\').head(10)\\\\n            validation = pd.read_csv(\\'../Data/validation.csv\\').head(10)\\\\n            test = pd.read_csv(\\'../Data/test.csv\\').head(10)\\\\n            if questions == \\'standard\\':\\\\n                if language == \\'english\\':\\\\n                    train = train[[\\'abstract\\', \\'question_en_orig