           ## Classification\\\\n    171:             ### Tokenizer\\\\n    172:             from transformers import AutoTokenizer\\\\n    173: \\\\n    174:             tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\\\\n    175: \\\\n    176:             def preprocess_function(examples):\\\\n    177:                 return tokenizer(examples[\\\\\"text\\\\\"], truncation=True, padding=True, max_length=512)\\\\n    178: \\\\n    179:             tokenized_text = my_dataset_dict.map(preprocess_function, batched=True)\\\\n    180: \\\\n    181:             from transformers import DataCollatorWithPadding\\\\n    182: \\\\n    183:             data_collator = DataCollatorWithPadding(tokenizer=tokenizer)\\\\n    184: \\\\n    185:             ### Train\\\\n    186: \\\\n    187:             from transformers import AutoModelForSequenceClassification, TrainingArguments, Trainer\\\\n    188: \\\\n    189:             model = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(model_name, num_labels=2)\\\\n    190: \\\\n    191:             training_args = TrainingArguments(\\\\n    192:                     output_dir=\\\\\"./results\\\\\",\\\\n    193:                     learning_rate=2e-5,\\\\n    194:                     per_device_train_batch_size=batch_size,\\\\n    195:                     per_device_eval_batch_size=batch_size,\\\\n    196:                     num_train_epochs=8,\\\\n    197:                     weight_decay=0.01,\\\\n    198:                     save_total_limit=1,\\\\n    199:                     overwrite_output_dir=True,\\\\n    200:                     load_best_model_at_end=True,\\\\n    201:                     save_strategy=\\\\\"no\\\\\",\\\\n    202:                     seed=42\\\\n    203:                 )\\\\n    204: \\\\n    205:             trainer = Trainer(\\\\n    206:                     model=model,\\\\n    207:                     args=training_args,\\\\n    208:                     train_dataset=tokenized_text[\\\\\"train\\\\\"],\\\\n    209:                     eval_dataset=tokenized_text[\\\\\"validation\\\\\"],\\\\n    210:                     tokenizer=tokenizer,\\\\n    211:                     data_collator=data_collator,\\\\n    212:                 )\\\\n    213: \\\\n    214:             trainer.train()\\\\n    215: \\\\n    216:             ## Prediction\\\\n    217: \\\\n    218:             results = trainer.predict(tokenized_text[\\'test\\']).predictions\\\\n    219: \\\\n    220:             test[\\'predictions\\'] = np.argmax(results, axis=-1)\\\\n    221: \\\\n    222:             ## Metrics\\\\n    223:             f1 = f1_score(test[\\'label\\'], test[\\'predictions\\'], average = \\'weighted\\')\\\\n    224:             acc = accuracy_score(test[\\'label\\'], test[\\'predictions\\'])\\\\n    225: \\\\n    226:             print(\\'F1-score:\\', f1)\\\\n    227:             print(\\'Accuracy:\\', acc)\\\\n    228: \\\\n    229:             result = [model_name, questions, language, f1, acc]\\\\n    230: \\\\n    231:             with open(\\'AT_results.csv\\', \\'a\\') as fd:\\\\n    232:                 write = csv.writer(fd)\\\\n    233:                 write.writerow(result)\\\\n>> Full file (233 lines, 2018 tokens)\"}\\n\\n[[ ## thought_9 ## ]]\\nI\\'ve inspected \"AT_finetuning.py\" and found:\\n- It loops over all models, languages, and dataset types, but I only need \"bert-base-uncased\", \"portuguese\", and \"standard\".\\n- The batch_size for \\'bert-base-uncased\\' is set to 16 by default, but must be changed to 1.\\n- Epochs are set to num_train_epochs=8, but must be set to 1.\\n- The script loads full datasets with pd.read_csv(\\'train.csv\\'), etc.; I need to select only the first 10 rows for each split immediately after loading.\\n- To ensure a controlled run, I will make a temporary edit to restrict the for-loops to just \"bert-base-uncased\", \"portuguese\", \"standard\", set batch_size=1, num_train_epochs=1, and slice train/validation/test to .head(10). This matches all requirements and avoids unwanted runs on other models/splits.\\nNext, I will edit \"AT_finetuning.py\" with these changes.\\n\\n[[ ## tool_name_9 ## ]]\\nedit_file\\n\\n[[ ## tool_args_9 ## ]]\\n{\"file_path\": \"Pira/Triggering/AT_finetuning.py\", \"edits\": [{\"find\": \"languages = \\\\\\\\[\\'english\\', \\'portuguese\\'\\\\\\\\]\", \"replace\": \"languages = [\\'portuguese\\']\"}, {\"find\": \"question_type = \\\\\\\\[\\'standard\\', \\'human_paraphrase\\', \\'automatic_paraphrase\\'\\\\\\\\]\", \"replace\": \"question_type = [\\'standard\\']\"}, {\"find\": \"model_names = \\\\\\\\[\\'bert-base-uncased\\', \\'bert-large-uncased\\',  \\'roberta-base\\', \\'roberta-large\\',\\\\\\\\s*\\'neuralmind/bert-base-portuguese-cased\\'\\\\\\\\]\", \"replace\": \"model_names = [\\'bert-base-uncased\\']\"}, {\"find\": \"if model_name in \\\\\\\\[\\'bert-base-uncased\\', \\'roberta-base\\', \\'neuralmind/bert-base-portuguese-cased\\'\\\\\\\\]:\\\\\\\\s*batch_size = 16\", \"replace\": \"if model_name in [\\'bert-base-uncased\\', \\'roberta-base\\', \\'neuralmind/bert-base-portuguese-cased\\']:\\\\n    batch_size = 1\"}, {\"find\": \"num_train_epochs=8\", \"replace\": \"num_train_epochs=1\"}, {\"find\": \"train, validation, test = pd.read_csv\\\\\\\\(\\'train.csv\\'\\\\\\\\), pd.read_csv\\\\\\\\(\\'validation.csv\\'\\\\\\\\), pd.read_csv\\\\\\\\(\\'test.csv\\'\\\\\\\\)\", \"replace\": \"train, validation, test = pd.read_csv(\\'train.csv\\').head(10), pd.read_csv(\\'validation.csv\\').head(10), pd.read_csv(\\'test.csv\\').head(10)\"}]}\\n\\n[[ ## observation_9 ## ]]\\nExecution error in edit_file: \\nTraceback (most recent call last):\\n  File \"/mnt/c/Users/2825425/work/gepa-research/gepa-modified/gepa_artifact/utils/dspy/dspy/predict/react.py\", line 91, in forward\\n    trajectory[f\"observation_{idx}\"] = self.tools[pred.next_tool_name](**pred.next_tool_args)\\n                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^